# Project Prompt — regenerate the site from scratch

You are generating a complete static photo-portfolio website. Follow this spec
exactly; the result must match the described site file-for-file, behavior-for-behavior.

## Context & identity

- Owner: "Kate" (Ekaterina Tsar), photographer based in Geneva, Switzerland.
- Single page, plain HTML/CSS/JS, NO frameworks, NO build tooling, NO external
  JS libraries. All JS is written inside one IIFE in `js/main.js` with
  `"use strict"` and ES5-style `var` syntax.
- Hosted on GitHub Pages from the repo root; must work with an empty
  `.nojekyll` file at root.
- Photo content and copy mirror the owner's old site etsareg.photos
  (bios, section texts, contact e-mail, Instagram, logo, ~74 photos).

## Repository layout (create all of this)

```
.
├── .gitignore                   (etsareg.com/, _site/, .DS_Store)
├── .nojekyll                    (empty file)
├── README.md                    (docs: layout, content pipeline, photo ops,
│                                 Actions, customization table, troubleshooting)
├── index.html                   (single page, described below)
├── galleries.json               (gallery metadata, exact content below)
├── project.prompt / this file   (spec)
├── css/style.css
├── js/main.js
├── scripts/build.py             (gallery generator, spec below)
├── .github/workflows/build.yml  (auto-rebuild on push, spec below)
└── images/
    ├── logo_wb_app.png          (white "Kate." logo, header)
    ├── favicon.png              (site favicon, taken from the old site)
    ├── me-1.jpg                 (self portrait, 3:4)
    ├── me-2.JPG                 (tall self portrait, used in About)
    ├── portrait/   9 jpgs: Portrait_E_B1..B3, Portrait_E_BW1..BW3, Portrait_J1..J3
    ├── creative/   17 jpgs: creative-1..5, creative_2-1..6, creative_3-1..6
    ├── events/     7 jpgs: event-1..7
    ├── street/     17 jpgs: p1..p9, street-2-2..street-2-9
    └── travel/     24 jpgs: p1..p24
```

If real photos are unavailable, generate placeholder JPGs with correct names,
portrait/square/landscape mix, 2048 px long side.

