## Design system (css/style.css)

Dark, elegant, editorial. CSS custom properties on `:root`:
`--bg #0e0f12; --surface #15171c; --surface-2 #1c1f26; --text #e8e6e1;
--muted #9a978f; --line #2a2d35; --accent #c8a35a;`
`--serif: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif; --sans: "Inter", -apple-system, sans-serif;`
`--header-h: 72px;`

- Fonts via Google Fonts link: Playfair Display (400/600 + italic 400), Inter (300/400/500).
- `html { scroll-behavior: smooth; scroll-padding-top: var(--header-h); }`
- body: bg var(--bg), color var(--text), font var(--sans), weight 300, line-height 1.7.
- `.container { width: min(1140px, 92%); margin-inline: auto; }`
- Buttons `.btn` uppercase, letter-spacing .18em, 1px accent border;
  `.btn-primary` filled accent (text #14110a) → inverts on hover; `.btn-ghost` outline → fills on hover.
- Section paddings `clamp(4.5rem, 10vw, 8rem)`; `.section-kicker` gold uppercase .75rem
  letter-spacing .3em; `.section-title` serif clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3rem).
- `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)`: kill html smooth scroll, reveal & gallery transitions.
- Responsive breakpoints: 900px (about & contact grids → 1 col; gallery 3 columns),
  620px (hamburger nav; gallery 2 columns; services list 1 col).

## Page structure & exact copy (index.html)

`<html lang="en">` — title `Kate. Geneva Photography`; meta description:
`Kate is a Geneva-based photographer for portraits, creative projects, events, street and travel — atmospheric visual storytelling with a soft cinematic look.`;
og:title/og:description/og:type + og:image (`images/me-1.jpg`);
`<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="images/favicon.png">`;
Google-Fonts preconnect + stylesheet; `css/style.css`.

1. **Header** `.site-header#siteHeader` (fixed, transparent → `.scrolled` gets
   rgba(14,15,18,.92) + backdrop blur + bottom line): container flex
   `.header-inner`; `.brand` = `<img class="brand-logo" src="images/logo_wb_app.png" alt="Kate — Geneva Photography">`
   (height 36px) linking `#home`; `.site-nav#siteNav` links Home/About/Galleries/Contact
   (muted → accent on hover, uppercase .85rem, letter-spacing .12em);
   `.nav-toggle#navToggle` hamburger (3 spans, X-transform on `.open`), aria-expanded.

2. **Hero** `.hero#home`: `min-height: 100svh`, centered text, `overflow: hidden`.
   - `.hero-slides` = absolute inset-0 flex strip, `will-change: transform`, NO CSS
     transition on it (movement is JS-animated). Children `.hero-slide`
     `flex: 0 0 100%` (position relative) each containing full-cover `<img>`
     (`object-fit: cover`), followed by a clone slide with `data-clone` (no
     data-gallery, empty alt).
   - Inside the strip, wrap the slides with markers:
     `<!-- HERO-SLIDES:START -->` … `<!-- HERO-SLIDES:END -->`
   - `.hero-overlay`: `linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(14,15,18,.55), rgba(14,15,18,.35) 45%, rgba(14,15,18,.85))`.
   - `.hero-content` (relative): kicker "Geneva-based photographer";
     `<h1 class="hero-title">Kate</h1>` serif clamp(3rem, 9vw, 6.5rem);
     subtitle italic serif "Portraits, events and quiet moments of beauty.";
     `.btn.btn-primary` → `#galleries` "View Galleries".
   - `.scroll-cue`: centered bottom, 1px × 52px gold gradient line, keyframe
     `cue` scaleY in/out loop 2s, links to `#about`.
    - `.slide-name#slideName`: caption block styled after the original
      bootstrap carousel-caption: absolute, left 15%, right 15%, bottom 85px,
      text-align right, white text, `text-shadow 0 1px 12px rgba(0,0,0,.55)`,
      no background/border, `transition: opacity .6s`):
      `<span class="slide-name-label">` (sans, uppercase, weight 500,
      letter-spacing 3px, clamp(1rem,2.2vw,1.35rem), margin-bottom 1rem) +
      `<span class="slide-name-teaser">` (plain, 1rem, #fff).
      On ≤620px: left 5%, bottom 5rem, teaser .85rem.
      Initial content = first gallery's title + sub.

3. **About** `.about#about` (bg --surface): `.about-grid` 2-col grid
   `minmax(0,.9fr) minmax(0,1.1fr)`, gap clamp(2rem,6vw,5rem). Left
   `.about-photo` img `images/me-2.JPG` alt "Portrait of Kate, photographer",
   `aspect-ratio: 3/4; object-fit: cover; object-position: center 20%`. Right
   `.about-text`: kicker "About me"; `<h2>` "Geneva-based photographer for portraits,
   events and atmospheric visual storytelling"; paragraph "I look for people,
   places and fleeting moments, capturing beauty all the while aiming for a soft
   cinematic look."; paragraph "Feel free to contact me to see what we can do
   together!"; `<ul class="about-services">` 2-col list with em-dash gold
   ::before markers: "Portraits — elegant & natural", "Creative projects & UGC
   work", "Events & gatherings", "Street & travel photography"; `.btn.btn-ghost`
   → `#contact` "Work with me".

4. **Galleries** `.galleries#galleries`: kicker "Selected work" + title
   "Galleries" (both `.center`).
   - `.filters` (role=group, aria-label): `<!-- FILTERS:START -->` buttons
     `.filter-btn` — `All` (`.is-active`, data-filter="all") + one per gallery
     (data-filter = folder name, label = title) `<!-- FILTERS:END -->`;
     underline-on-active style, no border/bg otherwise.
   - `<!-- GALLERIES:START -->` per gallery a `.gallery-group[data-group]`:
     `.group-head` with `<h3 class="group-title">` (serif clamp(1.5rem,3vw,2rem),
     gold 2.6rem underline via ::after) + `<p class="group-sub">` (italic serif
     muted); then `.gallery-grid` of `<figure class="gallery-item reveal"
     data-category tabindex="0">` — full-size `<img loading="lazy">`
     (alt `"<Title> photograph NN"`), `<figcaption><Title NN><span><Title></span></figcaption>`.
     `<!-- GALLERIES:END -->`
   - **Masonry**: `.gallery-grid { columns: 4; column-gap: 1.2rem; }`;
     `.gallery-item { break-inside: avoid; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; overflow: hidden;
     cursor: zoom-in; background: var(--surface-2); position: relative; }`;
     `.gallery-item img { width: 100%; height: auto; transition: transform .5s; }`
     (photos keep native proportions — NO fixed aspect ratios, NO gaps).
     Column counts: 4 at >900px, 3 at ≤900px, 2 at ≤620px.
     Hover/focus: `transform: scale(1.05)` on img; figcaption overlay
     (gradient bottom, serif title + gold uppercase span) fades/slides in.
     `.hide { display: none; }` for both items and groups.
   - `.reveal`: opacity 0 / translateY(24px), `.visible` resets, .7s ease.

5. **Contact** `.contact#contact` (bg --surface): `.contact-grid` 2 cols.
   Left: kicker "Get in touch"; title "Let's create something together";
   "Available for commissions and collaborations in Geneva, all of Switzerland
   and on travel."; `.contact-list` (Email → `mailto:photos@etsareg.com?subject=Photography%20inquiry`,
   Based in → Geneva, Switzerland; bordered rows, 90px uppercase muted labels);
   `.socials`: one link "Instagram · @etsareg.photos" →
   `https://www.instagram.com/etsareg.photos` target=_blank rel=noopener.
   Right: `.contact-form#contactForm` with
   `action="https://api.web3forms.com/submit" method="POST"` and hidden fields
   `access_key` (value `0e54d6af-dec1-4b34-b4c0-fec78965e813`), `subject`
   ("New enquiry from the website"), and honeypot checkbox `botcheck`
   (tabindex=-1, display:none) — labels uppercase .75rem muted; inputs/textarea
   bg --bg, 1px border var(--line), accent on focus, no outline; fields Name (text),
   Email (email), Message (textarea rows=5), all required with placeholders
   ("Your name", "you@example.com", "Tell me about your project…");
   submit `.btn.btn-primary` "Send message"; `<p class="form-note" id="formNote">`
   small muted: "Your message is sent straight to my inbox."

6. **Footer**: border-top var(--line); `.footer-inner` flex space-between wrap:
   `© <span id="year"></span> Kate · Geneva Photography · All rights reserved` +
   `back-top` link ↑ to #home.

7. **Lightbox** `.lightbox#lightbox` (role=dialog aria-modal, `hidden` attr,
   fixed inset 0, z-index 200, bg rgba(8,8,10,.94), flex center, `[hidden]{display:none}`):
   close × (top-right absolute), prev ‹ / next › big ghost buttons (2.4rem,
   opacity .7 → 1 & accent hover), `<figure class="lb-body">` max-width min(1000px,100%)
   with `<img id="lbImg">` (`max-height: 82vh; object-fit: contain`) and
   `.lb-caption` flex-between: `<span id="lbTitle">` serif + `<span id="lbCounter">`
   muted small uppercase; `body.no-scroll { overflow: hidden }` while open.

8. `<script src="js/main.js">` at end of body.

## Behaviour (js/main.js — single IIFE, ES5 style)

1. Sticky header: toggle `.scrolled` when scrollY > 40 (passive listener).
2. Footer year via `#year`.
3. Mobile nav: toggle `.open` on `#siteNav` + `#navToggle` + aria-expanded;
   close when a nav link is clicked.
4. Filters: on click set `.is-active`; toggle each `.gallery-group`
   `.hide` when `data-filter != all && data-group != filter`; same for items
   by `data-category`. (Group titles/filters are generated, nothing hardcoded.)
5. Reveal on scroll: IntersectionObserver threshold 0.12, add `.visible`,
   unobserve; fallback add visible immediately if no IO.
6. Lightbox: open on click or Enter/Space of item; operate on
   `visibleItems()` (items without `.hide`) so it navigates within the active
   filter; render() sets src/alt, title = figcaption firstChild, counter
   `"n / total"`; prev/next wrap with modulo; Escape closes; ←/→ navigate;
   click backdrop (target == lightbox) closes; body `.no-scroll`; restore
   focus to the tile on close.
7. Contact form submit: preventDefault; disable button; `fetch(form.action,
   POST, Accept: application/json, body FormData)`; on `json.success` reset the
   form and set `#formNote` to "Thank you! Your message has been sent." with
   class `sent` (accent color); otherwise/network-fail show a fallback note
   pointing to photos@etsareg.com; re-enable button.
8. **Hero slideshow** (must be frame-animated; no CSS transitions on the strip):
   - Collect `.hero-slide` elements (one per gallery + clone of first).
   - On load: for every slide with `data-gallery`, replace its img src with a
     **randomly chosen photo from the matching gallery** (pool = grid items
     whose `data-category` equals the slide's gallery); the `data-clone` slide
     copies slide 0's src (keeps loop seamless); then set chip label/teaser
     from slide 0's data-name/data-teaser.
   - Every **20 000 ms**, if not animating, slide the strip LEFT by one slide:
     rAF loop, duration **1600 ms**, easing `easeInOutCubic`
     (`t<.5 ? 4t³ : 1-(-2t+2)³/2`), applying
     `translate3d(-(from + (to-from)*ease(p))*100%, 0, 0)`; at completion, if
     the target was the clone index, instantly reset position to 0 and logical
     index 0 (never animate rightwards).
   - Chip cross-fade: opacity 0 immediately, swap texts after 700 ms, opacity 1.
   - Rotation must run even when prefers-reduced-motion is set (CSS simply
     keeps transitions off); do NOT gate the interval on matchMedia.

## scripts/build.py — generator (Python ≥3.8, stdlib only)

- Scans `images/*` subfolders containing ≥1 photo (`.jpg .jpeg .png .webp
  .avif`, hidden files ignored). Gallery id = folder name.
- Order & presentation from `galleries.json`; listed folders first in file
  order (only existing ones), unlisted folders appended alphabetically;
  missing config → title = folder name capitalized, empty sub (omit `.group-sub`
  line if empty).
- Photos sorted by natural key (digit groups as integers, then suffix).
- Generates three HTML fragments and replaces the content between
  `<!-- HERO-SLIDES:START/END -->`, `<!-- FILTERS:START/END -->`,
  `<!-- GALLERIES:START/END -->` in `index.html` (marker lines preserved):
  hero slides (data-name/data-gallery/data-teaser, first photo as static src,
  plus clone of first gallery with `data-clone` and `alt=""`), filter buttons
  (`All` first with `is-active`), and the gallery groups exactly matching the
  markup rules above (tile caption `"<Title> NN"`, span sub-label = Title,
  alt `"<Title> photograph NN"`, 8-space/10-space indentation).
- Escapes `& < >` in text and `"` in attributes.
- Idempotent: writes only when changed; prints report (`<folder> <n> photos "<title>"` + TOTAL).
- Exits with error message (non-zero) if markers missing, images/ missing, or
  no galleries found — never writes a broken file.
- Run manually: `python3 scripts/build.py`.

## .github/workflows/build.yml

- `name: Rebuild galleries & deploy to GitHub Pages`;
  `on: push: branches [main]` + `workflow_dispatch`;
  `permissions: contents: write, pages: write, id-token: write`;
  `concurrency: group pages, cancel-in-progress false`.
- Job `build`: checkout@v4 → setup-python@v5 (3.12) → `python3 scripts/build.py`
  → if `git status --porcelain index.html` non-empty: configure
  `github-actions[bot]` / `41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com`,
  commit `-m "Update galleries from images/ [skip ci]"`, push →
  assemble `_site/` (copy `index.html galleries.json css/ js/ images/ .nojekyll`)
  → `actions/configure-pages@v5` → `actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3` with `path: _site`.
- Job `deploy` (needs build): `environment github-pages`,
  `actions/deploy-pages@v4`, expose `${{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url }}`.
- GitHub Pages settings must be **Source: GitHub Actions**.

## README.md

Must document: repo layout; generated-vs-hand-written regions + marker list;
the "folder = gallery" rule; galleries.json semantics & ordering; day-to-day
add/remove/rename recipes; how the Action works and debugging when it doesn't;
local preview + rebuild commands; customization table (hero text, about, email
in contact list + Web3Forms access_key location, Instagram, logo, colors,
slideshow 20 s / 1600 ms); contact form via Web3Forms (key = public hidden
field, how to change destination inbox); custom domain (CNAME
`etsareg.photos`); troubleshooting table; ~160 MB total site → push via git
not web UI.

## Acceptance checklist

- `python3 -m http.server` + curl: `/` and every referenced asset return 200.
- `index.html` parses balanced; 5 generated groups; 74 tiles; 6 hero slides; 6 filter buttons.
- `build.py` run twice → second says "up to date"; dropping a new folder
  `images/weddings/` + photos then rebuilding adds filter "Weddings", group, hero slide.
- Hero: strip slides left every 20 s with eased ~1.6 s motion, Travel→Events
  wraps seamlessly, chip updates name + teaser with fade.
- Filters collapse to a single titled group; lightbox arrows cycle only the
  visible set, Esc/focus-return work.
